  // ── HOT-RENDER OPENING REPAIR (R4 #1, 2026-06-24) ────────────────────────────
  // The dedicated HOT opener directive is ignored ~94% (HOT_CRISIS selected →
  // COLD rendered). This is the deterministic backstop, mirroring the codebase's
  // "instruction didn't hold → repair" pattern (ROMAN:OBJECT-GATE, CALCIFIED-MOVE).
  // BOUNDED: Scene 1 only · HOT_CRISIS only · romance-forward only · ONE attempt ·
  // mandated anchor first-line + ending preserved · opening MOVEMENT rewritten
  // in-motion. Re-measures once; logs pass/fail; no loop.
  // ── OPENING-TEMPERATURE classifier (v2, Roman 2026-06-26: IN-MOTION-AWARE) ───────────────
  // v1 measured catastrophe-NOUN density (fired/ruined/scandal) vs anomaly-NOUN density
  // (envelope/message/file) and gave ZERO credit to live action — so an embodied confrontation
  // ("Elena burst in, shoved her phone at my face — I jerked back") scored COLD while "the board
  // has copies" scored hot-adjacent. HOT means "pressure is happening NOW", not "enough disaster
  // nouns". v2 credits the in-motion signal toward HOT (conservative: up to 2 signals, NOT an
  // auto-pass) so live pressure isn't drowned by container nouns. The gate + this classifier SHARE
