      var head = '\n\nEXEMPLAR DISCIPLINE (HARD — applies to EVERY bracketed or quoted EXAMPLE anywhere in this prompt): those example lines exist ONLY to show the SHAPE of a strong beat — the move, the structure, the level of specificity. They are NOT a phrase bank. Do NOT reproduce any example\'s wording, imagery, metaphor, or distinctive sentence construction — not verbatim, and not lightly reskinned. Take the MOVE and rebuild it from scratch in THIS scene\'s own concrete, character-specific language. If a line you write could be found (even approximately) in one of the examples, rewrite it. The examples teach HOW to write the beat; the words must be your own and new to this story.';
      // CROSS-STORY PHRASE COOLDOWN — rotation, not prohibition. Each entry's
      // status is computed from rarity (source weight + length + use-count) and
      // stories-since-last-seen, then bucketed into three tiers with separate
      // directive language. EXACT-wording recurrence is discouraged much more
      // strongly than OBSERVATION recurrence (the reskin family).
