  // both a 1st-person self-reference AND a 3rd-person pronoun for the
  // protagonist (matched to her gender). Heuristic but conservative — only
  // fires when both registers co-occur in ONE paragraph, which is the
  // canonical mid-paragraph slip the directive forbids. Returns null when
  // clean, or { hits: [...] } describing each offending paragraph.
