          rendering: 'Grounded anatomy and proportions, realistic musculature, clear expressions. All shadows must be rendered as soft gradients with smooth transitions; no hard-edged shadow shapes. Male figures carry grounded physicality: slightly larger hands and a stable, weight-forward stance emphasizing presence. Figures stand with wide, planted feet and lowered center of gravity — silhouettes read as rooted and immovable. Surface rendering emphasizes fine ink detail with subtle tonal variation; highlights appear as liquid, reflective accents rather than flat white shapes. Motion is depicted with restraint: even in dynamic scenes, figures retain composure and balance. Facial expression remains controlled and introspective; avoid open-mouthed shouting or overt emotional exaggeration. Overall mood carries a quiet, contemplative weight; action is present but never chaotic or explosive. Hands are deliberately composed: fingers often arranged in slightly unconventional but anatomically plausible positions, emphasizing gesture and subtle tension. Hands frequently remain visible and expressive within the frame. Eye focus is often slightly indirect or delayed: characters may look just past the point of action or hold their gaze a fraction off-target. Reactions are slightly delayed: posture and gaze may lag behind the moment, maintaining a fraction of the previous state before adjustment. Even in restraint, figures must retain clear physical presence: posture, gesture, or gaze should carry enough intent to anchor the scene and avoid visual passivity. Despite delayed reactions, character intent must remain legible: the viewer should clearly understand what the character is thinking or responding to.',
