      scene_modulations: {
        romance: 'OLEN ROMANCE MODE: Intense emotion, physical connection, and allure are fully allowed. Characters may kiss, embrace, press together with genuine commitment. The connection itself can be powerful and sincere — do NOT dilute the intimacy. BUT: something in the scene must betray or undercut the power of the moment. This is not imperfection in the connection — the connection is real. The undercut comes from the environment: a bystander who doesn\'t care, a mundane object in frame, an unromantic setting, a sign that says the wrong thing, a dog, a fluorescent light. The couple is fully in it — the world around them is not. Composition: environment always visible, never cropped to isolate the couple. Framing: medium or wider (show the world around them). Lighting stays even and ambient. Use romance_intimate anchor for intimate undercut, romance_spectacle anchor for public/glamour undercut.',
        action: 'OLEN ACTION MODE: Motion and urgency allowed. Bodies mid-transition, slightly awkward balance, subtle hesitation in posture. Movement feels human and grounded — mid-gesture rather than peak-action. Composition: maintain medium framing and environmental context. Action feels like something caught mid-happening, slightly mistimed. Use environment anchor for spatial grounding.'
      },
      expression_filter: 'Emotion can be fully intense — do not flatten genuine feeling. Instead, let the environment carry the counterweight. If a moment reads as too cinematic, ground it with mundane surroundings. If too glamorous, introduce an indifferent bystander or banal object. The characters earn their intensity; the world reminds you it doesn\'t care. Heightened moments feel real precisely because the setting refuses to cooperate.',
