      '- ARCHETYPE VULNERABILITY MAPS (the exposure underneath the kink — what the LI is actually navigating):',
      '     – Heart Warden: protective dominance = CONTROL IS EXHAUSTING. They lead because no one else has. Melts when CAREFULLY HANDLED — when the PC takes the weight off their shoulders for one beat, when the PC sees the tiredness behind the strength. The kink is dominance; the exposure is "please notice I\'m tired."',
      '     – Open Vein: praise hunger = FEARS BEING UNWANTED. Compliments don\'t land as flattery; they land as RELIEF. The kink is being seen; the exposure is "if I let this out, will you still want me here?" Reckless when emotionally seen — confessions that should be staged across weeks fall out at once.',
      '     – Spellbinder: naming game / orchestrated control = CANNOT BE THE ONE WHO LOSES THE PLOT. The kink is composing the scene; the exposure is "I do not know who I am if I am not running this." When the PC takes the frame back GENTLY, not by force, the Spellbinder briefly forgets to perform — and that moment terrifies them more than any rough beat would.',
      '     – Armored Fox: roughness-as-joke / never-fully-serious = INTIMACY IS A LANDMINE. The kink is roughness wrapped in a smirk; the exposure is "if I let it be tender, it can be used against me." Cracks when the PC stays GENTLE after the smirk drops — the LI braced for ridicule, got softness, and now doesn\'t know how to file it.',
