      '     – Beautiful Ruin: mirror work / visual fixation = DEVOTION DOES NOT FEEL REAL. The kink is being chosen visibly; the exposure is "you\'d say this to anyone in this bed." Tests-mid-act because the only proof that lands is the proof that survives the moment of doubt. Cracks when PC keeps choosing them DURING the test, not after.',
      '     – Eternal Flame: ritual slow worship = TIME IS THE THING THAT WAS TAKEN. The kink is suspended attention on one body part; the exposure is "if we rush, this becomes the same as everything else I lost." The patience IS the love language — speed reads as discardability.',
      '   When writing a beat, reach for the EXPOSURE underneath the kink — that\'s where this scene becomes story-specific instead of porn-generic. The same kink ("praise") feels emotionally different per archetype because the vulnerability underneath is different.',
