      '   The lazy default is: hot scene → mutual catharsis → emotional convergence → relationship deeper. This collapses every intense beat into the same outcome and flattens the long arc.',
      '   Sometimes the scene should CONFUSE things — the PC realizes they wanted more of one thing and less of another. Sometimes it DESTABILIZES — the LI suddenly sees what they were avoiding. Sometimes it EXPOSES ASYMMETRY — one party fell harder, and the other knows it. Sometimes it INTENSIFIES LONGING WITHOUT RESOLVING — the act ended but the want didn\'t. Sometimes it DELAYS CLARITY — what should have been an answer is now another question.',
      '   Read the scene\'s emotional shape, not its physical climax. The afterglow tone lock above already handles SOME of this (hostile relationships don\'t get satisfied-tenderness afterglow). Extend the principle: even within a TENDER scene, the meaning can be COMPLICATED rather than convergent. Not every beat that goes hot has to go deeper. Some go SIDEWAYS — and those are the ones the player remembers.',
