      '   • MUTUAL LAUGHTER — small, unguarded, at something neither expected. The LI does a thing, the PC says a thing, the laugh is shared. This is intimacy expressed as JOY, not as want.',
      '   • CHECKED-IN CARE (NOT friction) — the LI asks "you\'re still with me?" as TENDERNESS, not as interruption. Or the PC pauses to look at the LI\'s face. A check-in as a love language, not as a safety stop.',
      '   • SILENCE AS CONNECTION — a beat where no one speaks and the silence FILLS the room. Different from "awkward silence" — this is the silence of two people who don\'t need to explain.',
      '   EXPLICITLY NOT IN THIS SET: failed timing, real awkwardness, overstimulation, uncertainty about what to do, mid-scene rhythm breakdowns. Those break the fantasy and turn participatory romance into documentary realism — wrong register. The fantasy is preserved; what\'s added is BREATH, not FRICTION.',
