      CAREGIVER:  ['refills your glass before you notice it was empty', 'remembers how everyone takes their coffee', 'puts themselves between you and the cold draft without comment', 'asks the second question, the one under the first', 'feeds people when there is nothing else they can fix', 'apologizes for things that were never theirs'],
      BUILDER:    ['straightens the crooked frame on someone else\'s wall', 'has the right small tool in a pocket nobody knew about', 'explains a thing by drawing it on whatever is nearby', 'finishes your sentence with how it could be done', 'cannot leave a wobbling table alone', 'restates the plan back as steps before agreeing to it'],
      REBEL:      ['reads the rule aloud, then bends it a little', 'asks who decided that, and actually means it', 'sits on the desk, not the chair', 'names the thing the whole room is being polite about', 'is late on purpose by exactly five minutes', 'keeps one small forbidden comfort in plain sight'],
      SCHOLAR:    ['corrects the small fact nobody asked about', 'cites where they heard a thing, every time', 'annotates the menu / the brief / the map in the margin', 'stops to get the exact word before continuing', 'remembers the footnote, not the headline', 'asks a question three steps ahead of the room'],
      PERFORMER:  ['plays to whoever just walked in', 'tells the version with the better ending, not the true one', 'checks their reflection in any dark glass', 'lands the line, then scans for who caught it', 'turns a complaint into a bit', 'goes quiet the instant no one is watching'],
      GUARDIAN:   ['takes the seat that faces the door, always', 'counts heads when the group moves', 'says the rule even when it costs them the room', 'steps a half-pace in front when a voice rises', 'keeps the schedule like a fence', 'is the last to sit and the first to stand'],
      SEEKER:     ['stands like they are already half-packed', 'asks what is past the thing you are describing', 'collects the names of places they have not been', 'leaves the conversation a beat before it ends', 'romanticizes the road, never the room', 'keeps a window cracked in any season'],
      RULER:      ['takes the head of the table without checking', 'edits other people\'s plans as a courtesy', 'lets others carry what they could carry themselves', 'restates the room\'s decision as if ratifying it', 'keeps their own time and lets the room adjust', 'thanks you in a way that files you'],
      SURVIVOR:   ['sits where they can see the entrance', 'eats fast even when there is no hurry', 'pockets the extra roll / the spare battery', 'clocks the second exit on the way in', 'goes still rather than loud when surprised', 'trusts the favor more than the promise']
