    // ── ROMANCE ARC ENGINE (Roman 2026-06-01) ──────────────────────────
    // The PC\'s private_hope and the LI\'s attraction_manifestation are
    // generated in parallel by separate Haiku calls. Resonance between
    // them is invisible to the prose layer unless we surface it. This
    // helper names both fields side-by-side and tells Sonnet what the
    // three possible relationship shapes mean for the arc — fulfillment
    // (resonant), tension (dissonant), or discovery (orthogonal). The
    // failure mode is not dissonance — dissonance is a valid arc engine.
    // The failure mode is INVISIBILITY: the prose layer doesn\'t know
    // whether her hope and his offer point at the same emotional
    // satisfaction, so the arc has no load-bearing spine.
    //
    // Returns \'\' if either Bible is missing or the relevant fields are
    // not populated — non-disruptive when context is incomplete.
    function _buildRomanceArcResonanceDirective() {
      try {
        var pc = (window.state && window.state.pcBodyBible) || null;
        var li = (window.state && window.state.liBodyBible) || null;
        if (!pc || !li) return '';
        var hope = pc.private_hope && pc.private_hope.toString().trim();
        var manif = li.attraction_manifestation && li.attraction_manifestation.toString().trim();
        if (!hope || !manif) return '';
        var pcName = (window.state && window.state.playerName) || 'the protagonist';
        var liName = (window.state && window.state.loveInterestName) || 'the love interest';
        var lines = [];
        lines.push('');
        lines.push('═══ ROMANCE ARC ENGINE (HARD — Roman 2026-06-01 post-Bible resonance) ═══');
        lines.push('The romance arc has a LOAD-BEARING SPINE between two Bible fields:');
        lines.push('  ' + pcName + '\'s PRIVATE HOPE (what she secretly wants but has not let herself name):');
        lines.push('    "' + hope + '"');
        lines.push('  ' + liName + '\'s ATTRACTION MANIFESTATION (what his care for her LOOKS LIKE as action):');
        lines.push('    "' + manif + '"');
        lines.push('');
        lines.push('READ THESE TWO FIELDS TOGETHER. The relationship between them is the arc\'s LOAD-BEARING TENSION OR FULFILLMENT — three possible shapes:');
        lines.push('');
        lines.push('  RESONANT — his manifestation directly fulfills her hope. (Example: she wants "to stop performing competence for one whole evening" + he "shows up, remembers, fixes — never admits why" = his showing up means she does not have to perform.) Arc shape: GRADUAL RECOGNITION + EVENTUAL SURRENDER. The romance writes itself toward fulfillment. Use restraint — the satisfaction must be earned across the arc, not declared in Scene 1. Drop hints; let her notice; let her resist the noticing; let her finally let herself want what he is already offering.');
        lines.push('');
        lines.push('  DISSONANT — his manifestation accidentally FRUSTRATES her hope. (Example: she wants "to be wanted when she is not useful" + his manifestation is "protection that takes her specific shape" = his protection requires her to be the one needing, which is utility. He is offering exactly what she has already been receiving from everyone, in a slightly more attentive register.) Arc shape: NEAR-MISS + RECONFIGURATION. Either SHE has to articulate what she actually wants (and he has to hear it without defending his form of care), or HE has to discover the manifestation that fits her specifically (the one that does NOT trigger her core_contradiction). The romance arc IS the negotiation between her hope and his default offer. This is the most generative shape — write toward it.');
        lines.push('');
        lines.push('  ORTHOGONAL — his manifestation neither fulfills nor frustrates her hope; they operate on different axes. (Example: she wants "to find out the loyalty was real all along" + he "remembers what other people forgot they told him, years later" = the manifestations are compatible but they are answering different questions.) Arc shape: DISCOVERY. Each of them slowly learns what the OTHER is actually asking for. The romance arc is the unfolding revelation that they are not in the same conversation yet.');
        lines.push('');
        lines.push('IDENTIFY which shape this pairing has and USE the relationship as the arc\'s engine. Do NOT collapse it into "they are perfect together" (RESONANT-mode generic) or "they fight" (DISSONANT mis-rendering). The shape is specific to THESE two fields. The reader should be able to feel the arc-engine without you naming it.');
        lines.push('');
        lines.push('FAILURE TEST: if Scene 1 prose contains no trace of either field — her private_hope is not visible in her interior register; his attraction_manifestation is not visible in any moment she sees / remembers / hears about him — the arc engine is offline. The Scene 1 microdecision should naturally orbit one of these two fields (the question she is forced to answer touches her hope, or the moment she registers him echoes his manifestation). PHASE 1 INFLUENCE: weighted, not enforced; the prose layer is being TOLD the engine, not validated against it. If observed-live the engine is being ignored, we add teeth.');
        lines.push('═══');
        return lines.join('\n');
      } catch (_) { return ''; }
    }
    window._buildRomanceArcResonanceDirective = _buildRomanceArcResonanceDirective;

    // ── P3 (Roman 2026-06-01): shared planner-level romance context ──
    // Both Scene 1 scaffold and Scene 2+ skeleton needed direct awareness of
