              L.push('  • ROMANCE PRESSURE WITHOUT THE MAN (HARD — Roman 2026-06-04): "about her" is necessary but NOT sufficient. The person-shaped hole above is the PULL; this bullet is the missing INCOMING FORCE — the scene must LEAN toward the coming collision. Beyond establishing her vulnerability, tilt the scene toward an approaching, life-altering presence she has not met: her world is being MOVED by a hand she cannot yet see. WEAK (no lean): she is fired, end of scene. STRONG (leaning): she is fired — someone powerful is behind it — something is already coming for her — her life is being rearranged around an absence about to become a presence. The reader should finish Scene 1 EXPECTING the collision, oriented toward the incoming person. TWO HARD QUALIFIERS: (1) ROMANCE-shaped, NOT plot-shaped — the incoming force reads as a PERSON who will matter to her, never a case / mystery / document to be solved (that is the cold plot-fixation failure we fight); (2) OWNERSHIP preserved (HOT doctrine) — the force is felt through its effect ON HER, her own world moving under her, never an external object / envelope / folio she calmly examines AT a distance. Do NOT name him and do NOT have her recognize him — she has not met him; render INEVITABILITY + INTRUSION, not memory and not anticipation of a known man.');
