          'CRITICAL: DO NOT REQUIRE THE LI TO APPEAR ONSTAGE. The state can be enacted through any of seven presence modes; judge whether the prose enacted the state through the CORRECT presence mode for this scene, NOT whether the LI was face-to-face.\n' +
          'PRESENCE MODES:\n' +
          '  ONSTAGE              — they share the room; state via direct exchange.\n' +
          '  OFFSTAGE_MEMORY      — she carries a remembered specific of him; state via her relation to the memory.\n' +
          '  OFFSTAGE_OBJECT      — an object of his / from him is in the scene; state via her handling of it.\n' +
          '  OFFSTAGE_REPUTATION  — she knows OF him; state via how she resists / accepts / recasts the reputation.\n' +
          '  OFFSTAGE_FANTASY     — she imagines a version of him; state via what version she lets herself picture (or stops).\n' +
          '  OFFSTAGE_ABSENCE     — he is conspicuously not where the scene needs him; state via how the absence works on her.\n' +
          '  OFFSTAGE_A_PLOT_ECHO — the A-plot pressure carries personal meaning for BOTH; state via how she handles a pressure he is somehow inside.\n' +
          'Verdict:\n' +
          '  PRESENT — the state is enacted in the prose through a coherent presence mode; a reader would name the state.\n' +
          '  PARTIAL — traces surface but the state is weakly enacted, OR the prose tried a presence mode that does not work for this scene.\n' +
          '  ABSENT  — the prose does not enact this state in any presence mode; the scene reads as procedural/external.\n\n' +
          'JUDGMENT 2 — EMBODIMENT / TRANSLATION (Roman 2026-06-02 new audit target — translation, not planning).\n' +
          'Question: did the prose render the relationship state through CONCRETE SENSORY OR BEHAVIORAL DETAIL — or did it render it through EXPLANATORY narration about the LI\'s biography / history / what-the-point-is?\n' +
          'A relationship state can be PRESENT (judgment 1) and still be EXPOSITION (judgment 2) if the prose enacts the state by EXPLAINING the LI\'s past rather than rendering the state through detail the reader experiences directly.\n' +
          'Verdict:\n' +
          '  EMBODIED   — the state lives in concrete sensory/behavioral detail. A reader experiences the state through what is rendered, not what is told. The reader does not need biography to feel the state. Example: "She had forgotten the shape of his handwriting but not the shape of his omissions" — embodies recognition without explaining HIM.\n' +
          '  MIXED      — some embodied moments AND some explanatory passages; the prose alternates between rendering and telling.\n' +
          '  EXPOSITION — the state is delivered primarily through explanatory narration about the LI ("The point is that Roman abstained from..." / "He had walked out because..." / "The pattern was always X..."). The reader is being TOLD the relationship state rather than experiencing it. Even if structurally accurate, this is expository rendering.\n' +
          'How to tell: strip the LI\'s biography sentences from your reading. If the relationship state still lands through the surviving prose, EMBODIED. If the state collapses without the biographical sentences, EXPOSITION. MIXED if the state half-survives.\n\n' +
          'Return strict JSON with BOTH judgments.';
        var usr =
          'R-PLOT CONTEXT (what should be enacted in the prose):\n' +
          'Core tension: ' + (ctx.coreTension || '') + '\n' +
          (ctx.relationshipQuestion ? 'Relationship question: ' + ctx.relationshipQuestion + '\n' : '') +
          (ctx.escalationAxis ? 'Escalation axis: ' + ctx.escalationAxis + '\n' : '') +
          'CURRENT RELATIONSHIP STATE (this issue): ' + ctx.currentRelationshipState + '\n' +
          (ctx.nextRelationshipPressure ? 'NEXT PRESSURE: ' + ctx.nextRelationshipPressure + '\n' : '') +
          '\nSCENE PROSE:\n' + proseText.slice(0, 6000) + '\n\n' +
          'Return ONLY this JSON:\n' +
          '{\n' +
          '  "verdict": "<PRESENT | PARTIAL | ABSENT>",\n' +
          '  "presence_mode_used": "<ONSTAGE | OFFSTAGE_MEMORY | OFFSTAGE_OBJECT | OFFSTAGE_REPUTATION | OFFSTAGE_FANTASY | OFFSTAGE_ABSENCE | OFFSTAGE_A_PLOT_ECHO | NONE>",\n' +
          '  "reason": "<one sentence: which moments enact (or fail to enact) the state, and whether the chosen presence mode worked for this scene\'s setup>",\n' +
          '  "embodiment_verdict": "<EMBODIED | MIXED | EXPOSITION>",\n' +
          '  "embodiment_reason": "<one sentence: which specific prose moments render the state through concrete detail (EMBODIED) — or which explanatory sentences about the LI carry the state (EXPOSITION). Quote the load-bearing sentence in MIXED/EXPOSITION cases.>"\n' +
          '}';
        var res = await _auditPost({ temperature: 0.2, max_tokens: 500, messages: [ { role: 'system', content: sys }, { role: 'user', content: usr } ] });
        if (!res.ok) { try { console.warn('[R-PLOT:SCENE] HTTP ' + res.status); } catch (_) {} return null; }
        var data = await res.json();
        try { if (typeof _recordProxyTextCost === 'function') _recordProxyTextCost(data, 'gpt-4o-mini', 'audit'); } catch (_) {}
        var raw = (data && typeof data.content === 'string') ? data.content : '';
        raw = raw.replace(/^\s*```[a-z]*\s*/i, '').replace(/\s*```\s*$/i, '').trim();
        var lb = raw.indexOf('{'), rb = raw.lastIndexOf('}');
        if (lb === -1 || rb === -1) return null;
        var parsed;
        try { parsed = JSON.parse(raw.slice(lb, rb + 1)); } catch (_) { return null; }
        var _v = String(parsed.verdict || '').toUpperCase();
        var _r = String(parsed.reason || '').trim();
        var _pm = String(parsed.presence_mode_used || 'NONE').toUpperCase();
        var _emb = String(parsed.embodiment_verdict || '').toUpperCase();
        var _embR = String(parsed.embodiment_reason || '').trim();
        // Presence/coherence telemetry (existing)
        var line = '[R-PLOT:SCENE] ' + _v + ' (presence: ' + _pm + ') — state: "' + ctx.currentRelationshipState + '" · reason: ' + _r;
        if (_v === 'ABSENT' || _v === 'PARTIAL') console.warn(line);
        else console.log(line);
        // Embodiment/translation telemetry (Roman 2026-06-02 new audit target)
