'- DECK EXCLUSION (HARD): NEVER mention the protagonist\'s tarot deck, the cards, the Marseille deck, or "let the cards decide / draw a card" in ANY action or dialogue. The deck is a SEPARATE player mechanic (it has its own draw button), NOT a Say/Do option — keep it entirely out of every suggestion even though it appears in the scene. The protagonist holding the deck is NOT a reason to make handling it the action — suggest a REAL in-world action instead (use the scene\'s actual props, the protagonist\'s body, her voice, or — on a phone call — hang up / lower the phone / pace / go silent on the line). FORBIDDEN: "set the deck down," "put the cards away," "push the deck aside," "slip the cards into my pocket," "I\'m deciding this, not the cards," "before I draw a card," etc.' + (typeof _buildLanguageDirective === 'function' ? _buildLanguageDirective() : '');

