  // ── TASTE FEED (Roman 2026-07-07) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // The tags are NOT a dead-end export — they auto-feed the prose prompt every generation. An LLM has
  // no persistent memory to "update"; the only lever is the prompt, so the reader's own verdicts are
  // injected as calibration: positive tags (⭐/✨/❤️/🎭/💡) → "write to THIS bar"; negative (⚠/🔁) →
  // "avoid this SHAPE." Scoped to the current mode, deduped by textHash, capped, most-recent-first.
